‎## 4. Hypothesis — NOT YET ESTABLISHED — Needs Evidence
‎
‎**Statement:**
‎
‎> **Hypothesis — not yet established:** These frictions may be contributing to a broader shift toward multi-platform AI use and greater demand for portability.
‎
‎**Why not established:**
‎
‎Per [[KQ_INSTRUMENT_2026-08-26_Crossroads_Checklist]] checkpoint:
‎
‎> Has evaluation produced behaviour yet?
‎
‎- Complaints = Stages 01-02
‎- Evaluation begins = Stage 03 (comparing alternatives)
‎- Experimentation = Stage 04 (quietly testing other systems)
‎- Behaviour = Stage 08 (work diversified, workflows portable)
‎
‎We have not yet logged behaviour. We have logged friction.
‎
‎**To establish hypothesis, need:**
‎
‎- LOGs of actual diversification (users running same workflow across 2+ platforms)
‎- LOGs of portability work (exporting prompts, knowledge, projects to alternative)
‎- LOGs of migration (sustained shift, not trial)
‎- Metrics: multi-platform use increase, not just talk
‎
‎Until then: **signal, not migration.** Keeps KQ honest — your earlier command.
